{"step_index":991,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:33:56Z","thinking":"**Verifying Lemma Correctness**\n\nThe Lean 4 code compiles without errors, indicating the lemma is well-formed. The provided lemma `finset_min_getD_le` establishes a lower bound for an element of a finite set with its minimum value. The proof strategy hinges on showing the minimum is less than or equal to an element of the set using `Finset.inf_le`. This inequality is then case-split, and rewritten to deduce the desired result. The use of `WithTop` seems important for handling potential empty set scenarios.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nlemma finset_min_getD_le {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n    s.min.getD 0 ≤ b := by\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n  cases hm : s.min with\n  | top =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    simp at h\n  | coe m =>\n    rw [hm] at h\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n\nlemma radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [Dec